    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are primed for a high-ceiling outing today, headlined by **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, who carries our day-best efficiency score of 84.88 against a struggling Bennett. He benefits from a favorable matchup against a southpaw and a high-efficiency park factor, making him our primary anchor. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) and **Jackson Merrill** (74.56) are locked in as elite plays; both benefit from the defensive shortcomings of Avila and Leahy, respectively, with **Jackson Merrill** getting a significant boost from wind conditions pushing potential fly balls out of the park. **Drake Baldwin** also warrants attention, as his 72.68 score is driven by a plum matchup against Whisenhunt, where favorable wind and a strong spot in the two-hole position provide significant run-production upside.\n\nWhile the depth of the roster is impressive, the decision to leave **Brayan Rocchio** on the bench was a narrow call. His score of 53.93 fell just short of the threshold, largely due to the high-efficiency environment created by the rest of our core\u2014specifically the platoon and spot advantages held by **Curtis Mead** and **Liam Hicks**. We are monitoring the status of **Cole Carrigg** closely, as his 68.47 efficiency rating is threatened by a 43% rain risk in his contest against Assad; should that game face a delay or cancellation, **Brayan Rocchio** serves as our primary pivot. Meanwhile, **Gunnar Henderson** remains a vital piece of the lineup despite facing an elite arm in Kirby; his high base projection and favorable platoon dynamic justify the start even against a difficult pitcher profile.",
